window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-862c857e0358aa15"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"security-review\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"codex-security-review\">Codex Security Review 安全审查</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Enterprise、Business、Edu 和 Pro 用户可以使用 Codex Security Review；Plus 不支持此功能。安全审查会消耗套餐内包含的 Codex 用量或 ChatGPT credits。</p> <p>使用 Security Review 检查 GitHub 拉取请求（pull request）中的差异和相关代码，查找安全问题。如果已配置威胁模型上下文或安全指导，它会结合这些信息进行检查，并发布达到报告阈值的发现项。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">Code Review（代码审查）</a>在常规审查过程中也可能报告安全问题，因此两种审查可能报告同一条发现项。</p> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">开始之前</h2> <p>如需配置自动 Codex Security Review，你需要：</p> <ul> <li>在工作区中具有 Codex Security Review 使用权限</li> <li>已设置 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a>，并连接 GitHub 代码库</li> <li>对该代码库具有 GitHub 推送权限，或对其设置具有管理员权限</li> </ul> <p>已有的 Codex Security 扫描不是必需条件。</p> <p><a id=\"configure-security-review\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"configure-codex-security-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-security-review_1\">配置 Codex Security Review</h2> <p>代码库设置由所有人共享。更改这些设置会影响代码库 <strong>Review（审查）</strong>策略所选中的拉取请求，而不仅是你自己的拉取请求。如果代码库遵循个人偏好设置，那么个人偏好只会应用于你自己的拉取请求。</p> <ol> <li>前往 <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/settings/code-review\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex 设置（需联网）</a>，然后选择一个代码库。</li> <li>在 <strong>Review security vulnerabilities（审查安全漏洞）</strong>下，启用 <strong>Auto security review（自动安全审查）</strong>。</li> <li>使用 <strong>Review（审查）</strong>选择哪些拉取请求会进行 Codex Security Review：</li> <li><strong>Follow personal preferences（遵循个人偏好）</strong>允许每位贡献者通过个人 Codex Security Review 设置选择是否启用。</li> <li><strong>All PRs（所有拉取请求）</strong>适用于代码库中的每个拉取请求。</li> <li>如果提供 <strong>Team PRs（团队拉取请求）</strong>，它适用于由 ChatGPT 工作区成员发起的拉取请求，而不是由 GitHub 团队成员发起的拉取请求。</li> <li>使用 <strong>Trigger（触发条件）</strong>选择 Codex Security Review 的运行时机：</li> <li><strong>On PR open（拉取请求打开时）</strong>会在拉取请求打开时独立运行。</li> <li><strong>On every push（每次推送时）</strong>会在推送新提交后独立运行。</li> <li><strong>Whenever code review runs（每当代码审查运行时）</strong>要求启用 Code Review，并让 Codex Security Review 与它同时运行。</li> </ol> <p>将 GitHub 连接起来，或为其他贡献者启用个人审查，都不会额外请求审查你的拉取请求。是否运行自动审查取决于代码库设置和个人设置；系统不会针对每位已连接用户各创建一份审查。后续推送可能根据 <strong>Trigger（触发条件）</strong>再次触发审查，你也可以手动请求额外审查。</p> <p><a id=\"add-threat-model-context\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">添加威胁模型上下文</h2> <p>你可以配置威胁模型，向 Codex 提供应用资产、信任边界、安全假设和代码库特有风险等上下文。如果代码库已有 Codex Security 扫描配置，你可以使用其中的威胁模型；否则，请提供已提交到代码库中的威胁模型文件路径。如果不指定来源，Codex 会在每次审查时重新生成威胁模型。</p> <p><a id=\"set-reporting-thresholds\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">设置报告阈值</h2> <p>默认情况下，自动 Codex Security Review 会报告 <strong>High（高）</strong>和 <strong>Critical（严重）</strong>发现项；手动请求的审查会报告 <strong>Medium（中）</strong>、<strong>High（高）</strong>和 <strong>Critical（严重）</strong>发现项。你可以分别更改自动审查和手动审查的最低严重性级别，也可以添加基于路径的覆盖规则。</p> <p>发布到拉取请求中的发现项会继承该拉取请求的 GitHub 可见范围。任何能够查看该拉取请求的人都能查看这些发现项，包括公共代码库中的拉取请求，以及由工作区外部贡献者发起的拉取请求。报告阈值控制 Codex 发布到 GitHub 的内容。完整的 Codex Security Review 报告仍保留在 Codex 中。</p> <p><a id=\"request-a-security-review\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"request-a-codex-security-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-security-review_2\">请求 Codex Security Review</h2> <p>如需手动请求 Codex Security Review，请在拉取请求中添加以下评论：</p> <p><code>@codex security review</code></p> <p>审查运行期间，Codex 会作出响应；随后会直接在拉取请求中发布达到手动报告阈值的发现项。打开关联的 Codex 任务并选择 <strong>Security Report（安全报告）</strong>标签页，可查看完整报告，包括严重性、攻击路径、支持证据、验证情况和修复指导。如果没有问题达到报告阈值，Codex 就不会在拉取请求中发布发现项。将空评论结果理解为“审查已完成且没有发现项”之前，请先检查任务状态和完整报告。</p> <p><a id=\"related-docs\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">相关文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">使用 Codex 审查 GitHub 拉取请求</a>介绍 Code Review 和 GitHub 集成。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d5a186b7366ebd04\">Codex Security</a>介绍该产品。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Codex Security 云端设置</a>介绍代码库扫描和发现项审阅。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">改进威胁模型</a>介绍如何调整代码库上下文。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"security-review\">Security Review</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex Security Review is available to ChatGPT Enterprise, Business, Edu, and Pro customers. It isn't available on Plus. Security reviews consume included Codex allowance or ChatGPT credits.</p> <p>Use Security Review to check a GitHub pull request for security issues in its diff and supporting code. It uses threat-model context or security guidance when configured and posts findings that meet your reporting threshold.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">Code Review</a> can also report security issues during its general review, so the two reviews may report the same finding.</p> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>To configure automatic Codex Security Review, you need:</p> <ul> <li>Codex Security Review access for your workspace</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex cloud</a> set up with a connected GitHub repository</li> <li>GitHub push or admin permission for the repository settings</li> </ul> <p>An existing Codex Security scan is optional.</p> <p><a id=\"configure-security-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"configure-codex-security-review\">Configure Codex Security Review</h2> <p>Repository settings are shared. Changing them affects the pull requests selected by the repository's <strong>Review</strong> policy, not just your own pull requests. Personal preferences apply to your pull requests when the repository follows personal preferences.</p> <ol> <li>Go to <a href=\"https://chatgpt.com/settings/code-review\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Codex settings (online)</a> and choose a repository.</li> <li>Under <strong>Review security vulnerabilities</strong>, turn on <strong>Auto security review</strong>.</li> <li>Use <strong>Review</strong> to choose which pull requests get Codex Security Review:</li> <li><strong>Follow personal preferences</strong> lets each contributor opt in with their personal Codex Security Review settings.</li> <li><strong>All PRs</strong> applies to every pull request in the repository.</li> <li><strong>Team PRs</strong>, when available, applies to pull requests opened by members of your ChatGPT workspace, not members of a GitHub team.</li> <li>Use <strong>Trigger</strong> to choose when Codex Security Review runs:</li> <li><strong>On PR open</strong> runs independently when a pull request is opened.</li> <li><strong>On every push</strong> runs independently after new commits are pushed.</li> <li><strong>Whenever code review runs</strong> requires Code Review and runs Codex Security Review alongside it.</li> </ol> <p>Connecting GitHub or enabling personal reviews for another contributor doesn't request an extra review of your pull requests. Repository and personal settings determine whether an automatic review runs; they don't create one review per connected user. Later pushes can trigger another review according to <strong>Trigger</strong>, and you can request additional reviews manually.</p> <h2 id=\"add-threat-model-context\">Add threat-model context</h2> <p>You can configure a threat model to give Codex context about your application's assets, trust boundaries, security assumptions, and repository-specific risks. If the repository has an existing Codex Security scan configuration, you can use its threat model. Otherwise, provide the path to a threat model file checked into the repository. If you do not specify a source, Codex regenerates the threat model for every review.</p> <h2 id=\"set-reporting-thresholds\">Set reporting thresholds</h2> <p>By default, automatic Codex Security Reviews report <strong>High</strong> and <strong>Critical</strong> findings, while manually requested reviews report <strong>Medium</strong>, <strong>High</strong>, and <strong>Critical</strong> findings. You can change the minimum severity independently for automatic and manual reviews, and add path-based overrides.</p> <p>Findings posted to a pull request inherit that pull request's GitHub visibility. Anyone who can view the pull request can view those findings, including on public repositories or pull requests from contributors outside your workspace. The reporting threshold controls what Codex posts to GitHub. The full Codex Security Review report remains in Codex.</p> <p><a id=\"request-a-security-review\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"request-a-codex-security-review\">Request a Codex Security Review</h2> <p>To request a Codex Security Review manually, add this comment to a pull request:</p> <p><code>@codex security review</code></p> <p>Codex reacts while the review is running, then posts findings that meet your manual reporting threshold directly on the pull request. Open the associated Codex task and select the <strong>Security Report</strong> tab to view the full report, including severity, attack path, supporting evidence, validation, and remediation guidance. If no issues meet the reporting threshold, Codex does not post findings to the pull request. Check the task status and full report before interpreting an empty comment result as a completed review with no findings.</p> <h2 id=\"related-docs\">Related docs</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-ba7354e174823641\">Review GitHub pull requests with Codex</a> explains Code Review and the GitHub integration.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-d5a186b7366ebd04\">Codex Security</a> gives the product overview.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-10cdc56de63926b8\">Codex Security cloud setup</a> explains repository scans and findings review.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-0c53ef5188800731\">Improving the threat model</a> explains how to tune repository context.</li> </ul>"};
